# File: tests/features/add_greeting_utf16_length_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/317-add-greeting-utf16-length-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Return the UTF-16 code-unit count of the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count UTF-16 code units for BMP names
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_utf16_length is called with Ada and Zo plus U+00EB
    Then both results are 10
    And each result equals the UTF-16-LE byte length of the greeting divided by two

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Count a surrogate pair for non-BMP characters
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_utf16_length is called with U+1F600
    Then the result is 9
    And the result is one greater than greeting_length of U+1F600

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_utf16_length is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_utf16_length of Ada
    Then it prints 10 and greeting_utf16_length is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the UTF-16 code-unit count of the complete greeting and the inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0
